      "description": "Envoyer manuellement des payloads webhook TMF vers les BSS Gateways locales (comme le ferait le Hub)."
    },
    {
      "name": "Hub avec callback Postman",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Enregistrer Hub → callback Postman (BSS2)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const url = pm.environment.get('postmanWebhookUrl');",
                  "if (!url) {",
                  "  throw new Error('Renseignez postmanWebhookUrl (Collection → Integrations → Webhooks)');",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"callback\": \"{{postmanWebhookUrl}}\",\n  \"query\": \"PortabilityOrderOutValidationNeededEvent,PortabilityOrderStateChangeEvent\",\n  \"@type\": \"Hub\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{hubBaseUrl}}/portability/hub",
            "description": "Enregistre le Hub pour envoyer les webhooks vers votre URL Postman (`webhook.postman.co`). Puis créez un ordre port-in : Postman recevra le POST."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Créer ordre (déclenche webhook vers Postman)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.environment.set('orderId', pm.response.json().orderId);",
                  "console.log('Attendez quelques secondes puis vérifiez lastWebhookEventType dans l\\'environnement.');"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"requestType\": \"port-in\",\n  \"number\": \"5145559999\",\n  \"recipientOperator\": \"BSS1\",\n  \"currentOperator\": \"BSS2\",\n  \"customerInfo\": {\n    \"name\": \"Test Postman Webhook\",\n    \"accountId\": \"CUST-POSTMAN\"\n  },\n  \"requestedPortDate\": \"2026-07-21T12:00:00Z\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{hubBaseUrl}}/portability/order",
            "description": "Après enregistrement Hub avec callback Postman, le Hub envoie `PortabilityOrderOutValidationNeededEvent` à votre URL webhook."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "description": "Configurer le Hub pour livrer les webhooks directement dans Postman (nécessite compte Postman + webhook cloud)."
    },
    {
      "name": "Webhook entrant — traiter payload",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Parser webhook reçu",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const raw = pm.variables.get('request')",
                  "  || pm.collectionVariables.get('request')",
                  "  || pm.environment.get('request');",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Payload webhook présent', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(raw, 'Configurez un webhook Postman sur ce dossier').to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "if (raw) {",
                  "  const payload = JSON.parse(raw);",
                  "  pm.environment.set('lastWebhookEventType', payload.eventType || '');",
                  "  pm.environment.set('lastWebhookOrderId',",
                  "    payload.correlationId || payload.event?.portabilityOrder?.id || '');",
                  "  console.log('Webhook reçu:', payload.eventType);",
                  "  console.log(JSON.stringify(payload, null, 2));",
                  "  pm.test('eventType TMF connu', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(['PortabilityOrderOutValidationNeededEvent',",
                  "      'PortabilityOrderStateChangeEvent']).to.include(payload.eventType);",
                  "  });",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{hubBaseUrl}}/actuator/health",
            "description": "Cette requête est **déclenchée par le webhook Postman** (pas exécutée manuellement en principe).\n\nPostman injecte le corps du POST entrant dans la variable `request`. Le script Tests extrait `eventType` et `orderId`.\n\n**Setup** : Collection → ⋯ → Integrations → Webhooks → Add → cibler ce dossier."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "description": "Dossier à lier à votre URL `webhook.postman.co`. Quand le Hub POSTe un événement, Postman exécute ce dossier."
    },
